      "value": "<p>A very small icy moon with a smooth, bright, nearly uncratered surface that ought to be impossible on a body this old. The current explanation is a single resurfacing event of unknown cause within the last twenty million years, which implies a subsurface layer nobody has confirmed. It was named in the expectation of a second moon, which has not been found.</p>",
